.TH CHVT 1 "September 19, 2026" maux
.SH NAME
chvt \- switch virtual console
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B chvt
.I number
.SH DESCRIPTION
Switch the active console to number, from 1 through 4.
The command writes the maux console-switch escape sequence to standard
output. Its normal use is from a console:
.PP
.B chvt 2
.PP
Each console retains its own screen and shell context.
.SH FILES
/usr/man/CHVT  this page
.SH "SEE ALSO"
vidmode(1), sh(1)
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
Exit status is 0 for a valid request, 2 for a missing or invalid number.
.SH BUGS
Redirecting standard output writes the escape bytes into the destination; it does not switch the console.
